1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,500
Adherence OS is an AI decision layer for at-home GLP-1 care.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:15,400
It is organised as a care decision ledger: estimate next week's adherence interruption, show the evidence, compare one bounded support assumption, and review safely when rules detect a red flag.

3
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:23,000
Maya opens in Coaching mode. Eight weeks of synthetic history produce a five per cent interruption estimate.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Recent adherence is one hundred per cent, so one clear next action stays in view.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,200
The evidence map separates the highest-ranked context signal, the largest model contributor, and a bounded tested action.

6
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:41,200
Attribution separates model evidence, simulations, safety rules, and patient context.

7
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,000
Routine disruption accounts for thirty-two per cent of absolute local attribution.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,500
Selecting a node opens its provenance and exact local contribution without moving the decision canvas.

9
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:57,200
Now select Hydration nudge. This does not claim a treatment effect.

10
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:04,400
The app changes explicit feature assumptions, rescores the same monotonic model, and shows a two percentage-point scenario decrease.

11
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:10,000
The comparison appears only while every observed and simulated feature remains inside configured marginal bounds.

12
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:17,000
In Escalation, Maya reports severe abdominal pain, vomiting, poor hydration, and lightheadedness.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,500
Several features exceed their marginal bounds. Patient-specific ML evidence is withheld, and every tested action is suppressed.

14
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,200
Independent deterministic rules remain active and prepare an urgent local review draft.

15
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:36,000
Review drafts opens directly on Maya's local record.

16
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
It exposes the rule trigger, in-memory scope, and explicit delivery state: not sent.

17
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Red flags, context, the draft, and the audit trail are compressed for human review.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Nothing is diagnosed or sent automatically.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,500
The Check-in asks for the planned dose, four wellbeing scores, named current-symptom flags, mood, and short notes.

20
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:03,000
Deterministic safety updates immediately, then the app can generate a seven-day support plan with visible provider provenance.

21
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Field edits invalidate older requests, so stale provider work cannot overwrite the current decision.

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,500
The Model record makes the machine-learning boundary inspectable.

23
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:20,000
Its prospective target is the following week's planned adherence event.

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Patients are isolated across training, validation, and test.

25
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The record shows synthetic recall beside precision and review burden, then states exactly what the marginal-bounds gate cannot detect.

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Every metric is synthetic pipeline evidence, not clinical validation.

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,500
The same decision order works at three hundred and twenty pixels without horizontal overflow.

28
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:48,000
Patient impact comes from one clear action before adherence breaks.

29
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Innovation combines local ML, graph evidence, and independent safety.

30
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:58,700
The live story is simple: estimate, explain, test a bounded action, and review safely.
